<article class="env-lemma" id="081I">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/081I">Lemma <span data-tag="081I">29.26.16</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat morphism of schemes. Let $g : V \to Y$ be a quasi-compact morphism of schemes. Let $Z \subset Y$ be the scheme theoretic image of $g$ and let $Z' \subset X$ be the scheme theoretic image of the base change $V \times _ Y X \to X$. Then $Z' = f^{-1}Z$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that $Z$ is cut out by $\mathcal{I} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(\mathcal{O}_ Y \to g_*\mathcal{O}_ V)$ and $Z'$ is cut out by $\mathcal{I}' = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(\mathcal{O}_ X \to (V \times _ Y X \to X)_*\mathcal{O}_{V \times _ Y X})$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/01R8" data-tag="01R8">29.6.3</a>. Hence the question is local on $X$ and $Y$ and we may assume $X$ and $Y$ affine. Note that we may replace $V$ by $\coprod V_ i$ where $V = V_1 \cup \ldots \cup V_ n$ is a finite affine open covering. Hence we may assume $g$ is affine. In this case $(V \times _ Y X \to X)_*\mathcal{O}_{V \times _ Y X}$ is the pullback of $g_*\mathcal{O}_ V$ by $f$. Since $f$ is flat we conclude that $f^*\mathcal{I} = \mathcal{I}'$ and the lemma holds. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>